1
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:16,820
Everyone's being so uncooperative.

2
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:20,560
Maybe kanji was just
too much for us after all?

3
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:22,860
Don't say that now, of all times.

4
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:24,320
Reiko-san!

5
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:29,060
I know! How about selling
homemade cakes and cookies?

6
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,860
If we all pitch in,
we can still make it in time, right?

7
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:35,380
I'll cover the cost of the ingredients.

8
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:38,860
As expected of Reiko-san,
you're so reliable.

9
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:43,580
With all that screeching and peeping,
I can't even get any sleep.

10
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:46,180
You're hopeless, you savage.

11
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:49,560
Look who's come to slack off again,
you salary-stealing bum.

12
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:51,740
That's my line.

13
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:52,360
What?

14
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:55,020
Come on, Ryo-chan, help them out too.

15
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:59,260
Help? Them? Me?

16
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:01,040
No way.

17
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:02,080
Same here.

18
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:04,200
Right, like anyone would ever help you.

19
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:06,160
Now, now, you two.

20
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:11,460
Komachi-chan and the others can't gather enough items for tomorrow's bake sale,
and they're in a real bind.

21
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:13,760
Bake sale?

22
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:24,600
Someone's calling us.
That's Kameari over there.

23
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:27,900
Well, it's probably Kameari.

24
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:32,960
Everyone, come on over to our town!

25
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you.

26
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:39,360
Clash! Charity Bazaar!

27
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:44,480
Notice of the Charity Bazaar

28
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,380
I've never seen something like this before.

29
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:51,380
I put this poster up a whole month ago,
you know!

30
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:54,420
This poster?

31
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:58,140
A cheap-looking,
handwritten scrap of paper like this.

32
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:01,020
What did you say? How rude!

33
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:03,700
What is this? So lame, such bad taste.

34
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:06,820
With this, it's no wonder
the donations aren't coming in.

35
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:08,100
Komachi-key!

36
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:12,660
Reiko-san!

37
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:14,900
Please do something about that guy.

38
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:17,600
Worst, most terrible, super annoying.

39
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,480
That hurts, you know!

40
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:23,300
Ryo-chan,
Kei-chan and I cooperated too, you know.

41
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:26,960
Ryo-chan,
you must have plenty of toys you don't need.

42
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:31,620
Don't be ridiculous!
These are my precious treasures!

43
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:33,600
Not a single thing I own is useless.

44
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:37,140
Besides,
what do I stand to earn from some bazaar?

45
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:39,820
Idiot, this is a charity bazaar!

46
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:42,060
All the proceeds are going to be donated.

47
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:45,960
Why should I have to do
something like donate?

48
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,000
Egoist!

49
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,040
Lowlife!

50
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:50,240
What's with you two, you flat-chested pair?

51
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:57,540
Come on, Ryo-chan. This bazaar is meant
to help the neighborhood seniors' club.

52
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:03,740
When I was starving, not one of you gave me a single yen, and now you want to talk about
"going up in flames"?

53
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:05,520
Fine, Reiko-san.

54
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:10,160
Nobody's going to buy anything
from a barbarian like him anyway.

55
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:12,380
We don't need your help, so don't bother.

56
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:18,860
Don't be ridiculous! My collection is all
limited premium goods that fans would drool over.

57
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:25,160
Look, there are figures and limited programs here worth hundreds of thousands of yen,
all piled up.

58
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:27,540
We don't need your useless help.

59
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:30,220
Just don't get in our way.

60
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:32,680
And don't come to tomorrow's bazaar either.

61
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:33,820
You're a nuisance.

62
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:35,620
What?

63
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:38,940
Got it, Ryotsu Kankichi?

64
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:43,120
Shut up!
We're not taking orders from you lot.

65
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:49,960
Senpai, are you really sure
about selling all of this?

66
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:52,940
Figures and model kits too,
for when an emergency comes up.

67
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:55,300
I bought two of everything.

68
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:56,740
Just like you, Senpai.

69
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:03,660
Interaction with local residents

70
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:05,280
Also to deepen our faith

71
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,720
All temple staff, for the charity bazaar,

72
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:10,100
please actively cooperate.

73
00:04:10,780 --> 00:04:12,080
Alright, let's do this!

74
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,680
I'll buy all sorts of things.

75
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:15,540
There, I showed you the money, didn't I?

76
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:26,040
Just as I thought.

77
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:27,180
What do you mean?

78
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:28,820
It's "Komachi," but written in kanji.

79
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:31,520
After all,
this is all the selection there is.

80
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:35,840
Come on, come on,
step right up and take a look!

81
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:38,320
Here are treasures every collector must see.

82
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:41,640
We're selling super-rare
goods at super-low prices.

83
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:46,760
Ryo-chan's shop is the star
attraction of the bazaar.

84
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,400
Well, how about it, customer?

85
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:51,120
Mister, how much is this?

86
00:04:52,940 --> 00:05:00,520
It's a Miya model, so it's 8,000 yen.
8,000 yen is a bargain, you know!

87
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:08,600
How much is this? That one's 500,000 yen. If you let this one go,
you'll never see another one again!

88
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:17,640
It's really a good deal, I swear!
Senpai, isn't this a bit overpriced?

89
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:21,100
Don't be stupid! These are all items
that are nearly impossible to get now!

90
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:23,720
If you ask me,
it's an incredibly bargain price.

91
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,300
Welcome!

92
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:27,460
How about some decorative plates?

93
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:30,420
The soap sets are cheap!

94
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:32,620
We also have towel sets.

95
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:34,980
Seaweed, dried bonito flakes, and such too.

96
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:38,960
Sigh... Nothing's selling at all.

97
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:45,060
Looks like you've got a lot of free time

98
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,540
Kankichi Ryotsu

99
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:55,980
I told you not to come! Everything here is just leftover wedding
gifts and summer and year-end gifts from home that we're passing off.

100
00:05:55,980 --> 00:06:06,000
With stuff like this, nobody's even going to look at it! Shut up, what do you want us to do?
Everyone only donated junk like this, so what else can we do?

101
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:16,300
Well, in the end nobody really helped you lot seriously, that's all.
What's that supposed to mean? You talk like you could've gathered much better stuff yourself.

102
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:20,040
Anyone can talk big.

103
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:24,160
Fine, then let me show
you what I can really do!

104
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:27,020
Let's see it, then.

105
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:33,140
Yay!

106
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:42,780
This is no time to be eating leisurely!

107
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:44,420
What's going on here?

108
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:46,880
What did the chief donate to the bazaar?

109
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:49,080
A towel set, I'll have you know.

110
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:51,260
Towels? What did you say?

111
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:53,180
A towel set.

112
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:55,460
A towel set

113
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:56,780
Honda!

114
00:06:57,080 --> 00:07:00,340
Didn't Nakagawa donate an F40, right?

115
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:00,980
No!

116
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,520
Y-yes, that's right.

117
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:04,390
A Ferrari F40,

118
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:07,000
that's worth at least 50 million yen,
you know.

119
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,480
And a young whippersnapper
like Nakagawa donated it

120
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:12,500
What was it the chief donated again?

121
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:14,340
A towel set.

122
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:18,020
Reiko donated fifty designer bags,
didn't she?

123
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:19,940
I think that's right.

124
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:22,700
What was it the chief donated again?

125
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:24,600
A towel set.

126
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:29,300
At the Kameari box's bazaar,
what did their chief say he donated?

127
00:07:29,980 --> 00:07:34,740
Let me think... was it one million
yen's worth of home appliances?

128
00:07:34,740 --> 00:07:38,180
Yeah, one million yen's
worth of home appliances.

129
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:40,400
What was it the chief donated again?

130
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:41,740
(unintelligible)

131
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:43,820
What did you say?

132
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:49,580
That's right,
there were other donations too.

133
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:50,140
Right?

134
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:52,440
What should we take?

135
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:56,820
Nice watch you've got there, Chief.

136
00:07:56,820 --> 00:08:00,880
Oh no, this is bad.
I've only had it for three days.

137
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:03,460
Isn't that a Rolex?

138
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,800
Let's call it even with this.

139
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:09,820
Stop! I finally bought it with my bonus.

140
00:08:11,740 --> 00:08:13,700
Here's a premium cognac too.

141
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:16,600
W-why would you know about that?

142
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:19,880
You shouldn't be hiding gifts from visitors.

143
00:08:20,420 --> 00:08:22,640
Let's get everything out in the open now.

144
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:26,660
While we're at it,
let's take this gold cup too.

145
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:29,380
This is solid gold, so it's worth a lot.

146
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:35,660
Heh, this should be
enough to save face, Chief.

147
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:37,960
Thanks for your cooperation!

148
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:42,920
You devil!

149
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:45,900
What did the Chief donate?

150
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,480
It's a soap gift set, though.

151
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:50,880
A soap gift set

152
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:53,740
Is there a problem with that?

153
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:58,340
Station Chief Honda donated a Rolex,
didn't he?

154
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:02,740
Yes, and plenty of other
gifts and gold medals.

155
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:04,840
Wow, our boss is so generous!

156
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:08,120
By the way, what did the Chief donate again?

157
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:13,220
Well, I did put some thought into it,
you know.

158
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:15,340
You're donating that?

159
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:18,940
Didn't you have a golf set
that's just the right size?

160
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:22,600
Hold on!

161
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,760
No, this won't do.

162
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:27,980
Is it really okay to bring
something like this today, Chief?

163
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:28,560
That's...

164
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:33,580
The story about seeing the Chief at
the driving range during work hours.

165
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:35,500
Who did I hear that from again?

166
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:39,020
Hey, what would happen if it
reached the station chief's ears?

167
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:46,800
Thank you so much for your cooperation!

168
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:52,760
Even though I never used it once,
I appreciate your cooperation.

169
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:56,480
It's only a little, so...

170
00:09:57,160 --> 00:10:01,720
It's pricey,
but I'd rather pay in installments.

171
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:02,400
What?!

172
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:05,300
You're the best, senpai.

173
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:07,900
With this,
we'll rake in the cash, gapu gapu!

174
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:12,180
Let me show you how a real bazaar is done.

175
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:17,020
Step right up, come on over and take a look!

176
00:10:17,020 --> 00:10:20,760
Here we have Kakuno Department Store,
Akagiya, Shirakiya, and Kurokiya!

177
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:23,960
Just ask the lady wearing the red lipstick,
"Please give me one," and...

178
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:26,300
Fifty thousand, a hundred thousand, I'm not fussy about that.
Step right up, folks!

179
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:29,860
Hey, you know, today's a charity bazaar!

180
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:33,040
If you're paying that much,
I won't complain, damn it!

181
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:36,380
Rolex! How much is this?

182
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:38,780
Ten thousand yen?!

183
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:40,200
Is it genuine?

184
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:43,340
We're the police! We'd never sell fakes!

185
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:46,340
Here you go, 10,000 yen.

186
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:47,480
My darling.

187
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,920
This fishing rod?

188
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:52,280
Everything here is 10,000 yen,
no matter what.

189
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:53,240
No way.

190
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:53,920
Seriously, seriously.

191
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:54,900
I'll buy it!

192
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:55,700
Sold!

193
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:57,040
Me too! Me too!

194
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:58,520
Me too! Me too!

195
00:10:58,700 --> 00:10:59,440
Me too! Me too!

196
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:00,440
What about me?

197
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,920
Here you go, my darling.

198
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:02,760
Thank you very much.

199
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:06,780
10,000 yen, easy money.

200
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:42,240
What's all this? So many brand-name goods.

201
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:46,080
Everyone in the traffic division got
these from their boyfriends and such.

202
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,000
That's right.

203
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:51,600
Isn't this one still unopened?
How do you know what's inside?

204
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:53,900
Because we already have the same ones.

205
00:11:53,900 --> 00:11:56,960
When you get this many,
you just learn to tell.

206
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:59,080
Put yourself in the shoes
of the guy who sent them.

207
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:01,260
But we don't need them.

208
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:02,300
Hey.

209
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:05,360
I can't understand the guys
who lavish gifts on you lot.

210
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,740
Sour grapes.

211
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:10,420
Ordinary folks are in the way!
Shoo, shoo, go on over there!

212
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:11,640
What?

213
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:14,860
This is the real power of
the Traffic Division's guys.

214
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:17,420
Ahahaha!

215
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:19,700
No way!

216
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:22,700
The women at Katsushika station are really popular,
you know.

217
00:12:23,220 --> 00:12:26,860
What are you doing, Honda?
Who's minding the stall?

218
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:28,860
Well, that's the thing...

219
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:33,420
We've got nothing left to sell.

220
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:38,360
How much did we make in sales?

221
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:40,240
Let's see...

222
00:12:42,260 --> 00:12:44,240
It's exactly 250,000 yen.

223
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:53,480
None left.

224
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:55,680
Welcome!

225
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:57,640
Thank you for your purchase.

226
00:12:58,540 --> 00:12:59,940
Sorry, you're out of luck.

227
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:02,040
We sold more than you, didn't we?

228
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:16,400
My poor friends, long time no see!

229
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:17,760
There it is.

230
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:21,600
That's Shiratori Reiji.

231
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:27,220
Look, white!

232
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:32,240
Damn, I fell for it again.

233
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:35,240
Hey there, super-poor Ryotsu-kun.

234
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:38,940
Have my Porsche brought around to the parking lot,
would you?

235
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:41,360
I'm not your chauffeur, you know.

236
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:45,740
Reiko, thank you for inviting me today.

237
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:48,520
I hear it's a charity bazaar.

238
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:51,560
If you'd just said so,
I'd have helped as much as you like.

239
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:55,520
Well then, I suppose we'll let you help.

240
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:58,360
Name as much as you like,
as many as you want.

241
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:00,380
That card is a bit...

242
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:04,520
Same old idiotic book

243
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:06,840
This is exactly why I hate
the old downtown areas.

244
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:08,940
By the way, Reiko.

245
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:10,240
The one that opened in Odaiba -

246
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:14,640
If you're so eager to help,
then let's have you do it.

247
00:14:15,140 --> 00:14:18,840
Almost completely sold out.

248
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:21,560
This is all that's left unsold.

249
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:23,620
I'll take it all.

250
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:26,200
What are you going to do with high heels?

251
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:28,940
I just want to help the charity, that's all.

252
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:30,880
That's 3,000 yen.

253
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:31,920
3,000 yen, got it.

254
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:35,240
Wait, this is toy money!

255
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:37,514
If you come to my company later,

256
00:14:37,564 --> 00:14:41,200
I'll exchange it for real cash.
Cute Cinderella.

257
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,620
What? This is ridiculous!
Give it here! Give it here!

258
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:53,540
Look.

259
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:56,820
28, 29, 30...

260
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:58,620
Right, so this is the key.

261
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:03,020
With this, you're the owner now.

262
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:05,660
Wait, wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait, wait!

263
00:15:05,660 --> 00:15:07,760
This is my Porsche!

264
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:13,280
Sorry, but the ownership of this car has
just been transferred to him for 300,000 yen.

265
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,660
Don't mess with me!

266
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:15,980
Come on, quickly, while we still can.

267
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:16,720
Hey, look!

268
00:15:19,700 --> 00:15:21,100
My Porsche...

269
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,700
I'll just go collect the
high-heel money later after all.

270
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:29,300
Back to square one, then.

271
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:32,280
If that's the case,
you'd better help us out all the way.

272
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:35,360
Karomani suits.

273
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:37,440
Pulnari watches.

274
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,780
Miragamo shoes.

275
00:15:39,220 --> 00:15:41,340
Every single one is 10,000 yen!

276
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:43,640
Thank you for your purchase.

277
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:44,220
Thank you very much.

278
00:15:49,140 --> 00:15:50,460
Mommy!

279
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:55,360
That's an extra 100,000 yen right there!

280
00:15:55,360 --> 00:16:02,180
Welcome!

281
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:05,800
Would you like a homemade cake?

282
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:09,400
It's a cake shaped like a mini patrol car.

283
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:18,720
Aaaaaah!

284
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:26,360
Here comes that trick again.
Excuse me, coming through!

285
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,040
Yay!

286
00:16:40,580 --> 00:16:41,460
Cheers!

287
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:44,000
Genuine used uniforms, big clearance!

288
00:16:44,620 --> 00:16:48,200
How about this genuine uniform,
soaked with sweat and scent?

289
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:49,340
Is that the real thing?

290
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:50,860
Isn't it just a costume or something?

291
00:16:50,860 --> 00:16:53,640
Look closely,
it even has the name tag, right?

292
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:56,260
That's our uniform.

293
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,960
Hey! What are you going
to do about Gaian's Peck?

294
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,900
Yes, there's only one choice, right?
Do it early.

295
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:07,020
Thank you, Gaian.

296
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:11,280
Thank you for your cooperation.

297
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,680
This criminal!

298
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:18,320
Scary as he is, what a fool he is,

299
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:19,120
Chief!

300
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:21,720
You idiots!

301
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:23,840
Go get it back right now!

302
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:24,200
Yes!

303
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:24,420
Yes.

304
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:27,420
Hey,

305
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:29,860
go cool your head outside.

306
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:30,900
Serves you right.

307
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,980
Don't think this settles the contest.

308
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:35,680
You still want to go at it?

309
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:44,600
Today, I'm going to introduce some
wonderful products to all of you.

310
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:48,320
Here we have this
perfectly ordinary kotatsu.

311
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,640
What's this, anyway?

312
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:56,660
This is a kotatsu with a storied past. They say
DiCaprio used it during the filming of Titanic.

313
00:17:58,620 --> 00:18:04,140
Is it really that amazing? It must cost a fortune.
Come on, give it to us straight: how much?

314
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:05,660
For 4,800 yen.

315
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:09,400
That's a bargain, folks!

316
00:18:10,180 --> 00:18:12,920
And that's the kotatsu he
brought from his senpai's room.

317
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:15,700
What's that guy up to this time?

318
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:17,940
Next up, this toilet seat.

319
00:18:17,940 --> 00:18:21,620
This was a gift from a big-shot actor.

320
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:24,760
With this, you too can become a
big-shot toilet actor from today!

321
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:27,520
And it's still just a toilet seat.

322
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:29,500
That phony bastard.

323
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:31,260
Let's just leave him alone already.

324
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:33,300
No way I'm losing to a guy like that!

325
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:34,320
Help?

326
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:36,280
Of course, we'd be happy to help.

327
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:37,380
Just say the word.

328
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,540
Actually,

329
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:50,620
Well, well! This is a genuine Lautrec!

330
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:52,780
It was a gift I got for my birthday.

331
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:54,760
How much are you planning to sell it for?

332
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:57,160
Three million yen.

333
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:57,940
What!

334
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:00,020
Isn't that too expensive?

335
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:00,880
Do you think so?

336
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:02,640
Then one million yen.

337
00:19:04,380 --> 00:19:10,440
What!

338
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:11,820
Eight million!

339
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:12,780
Any other bids?

340
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:13,540
Eight million!

341
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:16,080
You've got Nakagawa and Reiko in your pocket

342
00:19:16,620 --> 00:19:17,600
Let's give up.

343
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:20,380
The money's all gone,
and there's nothing left to sell, man.

344
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:21,920
No, there's still something.

345
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:28,340
A 1LDK with a Japanese-style and Western-style room,
plus kitchen and toilet.

346
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:29,960
A detached single-story house with land.

347
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,060
Next door, they're selling
something at an unbelievable price.

348
00:19:32,060 --> 00:19:35,040
25 million yen is definitely cheap.

349
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:37,860
Selling off items and such.

350
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:38,900
Me too.

351
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:40,980
No idea, no idea.

352
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:43,120
Right now, a yacht is 3 million yen.

353
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:48,120
After all, this property was a former police station,
so it's built sturdy.

354
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:50,360
How about a helicopter?

355
00:19:51,260 --> 00:19:54,000
After all, it used to be a police dormitory.

356
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,180
The bath and the dining hall are huge, too.

357
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:57,140
Sold!

358
00:19:57,140 --> 00:19:58,020
Sold!

359
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:05,760
What a persistent guy.

360
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:07,480
Can't we just call it a draw by now?

361
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:10,000
Yeah, we've got nothing left to sell anyway.

362
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:11,520
No way!

363
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:12,505
Hey,

364
00:20:12,555 --> 00:20:16,040
Come at us from any direction

365
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:16,900
Senpai.

366
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:19,580
If it comes to this,
it's our final showdown.

367
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:20,760
Bring it on.

368
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:25,120
So, how do we settle it?

369
00:20:25,180 --> 00:20:26,080
Yakyuken.

370
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:27,460
Yakyuken?

371
00:20:28,180 --> 00:20:29,960
It's not just plain yakyuken.

372
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:32,860
Whoever loses the rock-paper-scissors
buys the other's clothes.

373
00:20:32,860 --> 00:20:34,540
That'll settle it once and for all.

374
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:35,500
Fine by me.

375
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:37,560
But if we're doing it,
we're going all the way.

376
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:38,720
Bring it on.

377
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Now, we shall begin the baseball conference.

378
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,320
Alright, let's give it a go.

379
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:51,080
If we're playing baseball,

380
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:54,300
let's do it this way.

381
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:55,640
I won!

382
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:56,420
Showdown!

383
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:58,940
I won!

384
00:20:58,940 --> 00:20:59,760
Lose...

385
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:05,560
The winner takes one off, right?

386
00:21:05,560 --> 00:21:06,720
I see.

387
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:08,460
Here's 10,000 yen.

388
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:13,960
I wonder how the bazaar is doing.

389
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:17,540
What's that?

390
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:18,120
Well...

391
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:19,700
Seven!

392
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:21,760
Cut!

393
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:23,560
I lost.

394
00:21:23,560 --> 00:21:25,200
Here's 10,000 yen.

395
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:38,340
This is the final showdown.

396
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:39,500
Alright!

397
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:44,320
If we're doing rock-paper-scissors,

398
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:47,140
let's do it this way.

399
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:49,420
Count, safe!

400
00:21:49,420 --> 00:21:51,100
Gai, gai, gai, gai!

401
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:51,940
I won!

402
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:55,280
Yes!

403
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:58,460
Strip, strip, strip!

404
00:21:58,460 --> 00:22:01,180
Strip, strip, strip!

405
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,820
Here, ten thousand yen.

406
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:05,920
Let's get you to take it off quickly.

407
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:06,820
Komachi

408
00:22:06,820 --> 00:22:09,900
If you're not going to follow the rules,

409
00:22:13,240 --> 00:22:14,200
I'll take it off, then.

410
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:15,500
Fine, I'll take it off, then.

411
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:18,580
Wait.

412
00:22:18,580 --> 00:22:19,620
Hold on.

413
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:25,180
It's not just the bulge in my crotch.

414
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:28,780
Special Investigator Kaipande, present!

415
00:22:28,780 --> 00:22:29,700
You

416
00:22:29,700 --> 00:22:31,540
I already understand the situation.

417
00:22:32,820 --> 00:22:35,040
Now that I'm here, everything's fine.

418
00:22:35,040 --> 00:22:35,960
Let's go.

419
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:38,300
Uniform!

420
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:42,120
On the lady's behalf,
I'll take off a layer myself.

421
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:43,300
N-no way!

422
00:22:47,260 --> 00:22:49,860
There's no point in you getting involved,
you know!

423
00:22:52,060 --> 00:22:53,940
In the end, no winner was decided.

424
00:22:53,940 --> 00:22:55,900
With 200 million yen in bazaar profits,

425
00:22:55,900 --> 00:22:58,640
the senior citizens' association
took a round-the-world cruise,

426
00:22:58,640 --> 00:23:01,040
a super-luxurious Nyan trip.

427
00:23:01,720 --> 00:23:02,120
And then

428
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:11,700
Senior... the Katsushika police box?

429
00:23:11,840 --> 00:23:12,540
Crap.

430
00:23:13,300 --> 00:23:14,540
Gyōzu

431
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:21,720
Gyōzu

432
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:23,060
Gyōzu

433
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:25,640
You...

434
00:23:26,180 --> 00:23:27,480
Not just the Katsushika police box,

435
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:31,600
but you sold off the Hasshutsujo
and the Nikoniko Dorm too, I hear.

436
00:23:31,600 --> 00:23:33,980
Well, that's

437
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:37,660
So how do you plan to take responsibility?

438
00:23:38,300 --> 00:23:39,640
Don't worry, Chief.

439
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:43,500
If we hold another Katsushika
Goods Relief Charity Bazaar,

440
00:23:43,500 --> 00:23:46,380
we'll easily raise 200 or 300 million yen!

441
00:23:46,380 --> 00:23:48,740
I'll handle everything, so rest assured.

442
00:23:48,740 --> 00:23:51,180
And we'll split the profits, of course.

443
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:53,440
Idiot!

444
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:57,080
Won't somebody rescue me?

445
00:24:01,120 --> 00:24:05,580
Kicking the alarm clock away, my pinky toe goes
"ow ow!"

446
00:24:07,260 --> 00:24:13,960
Draw my eyebrows, just for now,
then dash to the station, dash, dash, dash!

447
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:19,420
Packed train, a quick nap on Dad's back.

448
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:25,900
Another tough week, thanks for your hard work.
Overwork is only natural.

449
00:24:27,060 --> 00:24:33,300
Getting by with a baguette in one hand, but it's
beef bowl with extra sauce, cloudy and soupy.

450
00:24:33,900 --> 00:24:40,300
Endless overtime stress,
cleared right up by more irritation.

451
00:24:43,660 --> 00:24:50,080
Every day's a no-problem blend,
once I pass through a hot shower.

452
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:56,680
Every day's no-problem brain,
my sleep pillow restores my energy.

453
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:06,280
Every day's no-problem brain,
I love a girl like me.

454
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:13,080
Every day's no-problem brain,
hearts flying on Monday.

455
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:17,380
Magic, no-problem brain.

456
00:25:20,480 --> 00:25:21,880
The Olympics are coming soon.

457
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:23,880
It's about time Higurashi woke up, too.

458
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:24,500
went and did it.

459
00:25:24,500 --> 00:25:27,020
Didn't I go and spend the
money I borrowed from Higurashi?

460
00:25:27,020 --> 00:25:29,840
Wait, if I use Higurashi's psychic powers,

461
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:32,220
I can pay him back and make
a huge profit on top of it.

462
00:25:32,220 --> 00:25:33,900
I'm so clever.

463
00:25:34,520 --> 00:25:35,160
Next time:

464
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:37,920
"Hibernating Cop," see you again, okay?

465
00:25:38,660 --> 00:25:40,600
That's Kameari over there.

466
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:43,880
Tomorrow, it's Kameari.

467
00:25:45,600 --> 00:25:47,200
Come on, everyone,

468
00:25:47,200 --> 00:25:49,120
to our town!

469
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:50,820
Thank you.

